\paragraph{Guidance for future research.}
The evidence gradient (strong for OT-7B, moderate for R1-8B and QwQ-32B, qualified for R1-32B) indicates that distillation and native reasoning training produce qualitatively different safety representation geometry within the same architecture. PCA capacity control, control task selectivity, and position residualization (3/4 models retain significant non-positional HS advantage; \cref{app:position_residual}) provide converging evidence of genuine safety representations, but our probing approach is correlational. Causal validation via distributed alignment search~\citep{geiger2025causal}, LEACE~\citep{belrose2023leace}, or inference-time intervention~\citep{li2024iti} is necessary to confirm that probed directions are causally active rather than read-only features.

\paragraph{Layer selection audit protocol.}
We recommend five steps for probing studies with threshold-dependent metrics: (1)~train probes across all layers; (2)~compute $\geq$3 metrics per layer (threshold-free and threshold-dependent); (3)~check for metric disagreement in layer selection; (4)~report 2nd/3rd best layer results; (5)~compute cosine volatility (\cref{app:cosine_volatility}) as a crossing-rate bias diagnostic. Steps 3--5 cost negligible compute.

\paragraph{Hyperparameter selection.}
Layer (up to 64), $W$ (7 values), $K$ (5 values), and threshold are selected on the same validation set ($n{=}4$--$9$ per-class at 32B), yielding up to $2{,}240$ configurations. $C$-insensitivity (${<}2$pp) covers one axis; the cumulative degrees of freedom are substantial. $K$ was pre-selected (\cref{app:k_ablation}); joint (layer, $W$) stability was verified for QwQ-32B (\cref{app:layer_sweep}) but not R1-32B. Bootstrap CIs at $n{=}19$--$20$ may exhibit below-nominal coverage~\citep{efron1993bootstrap}.

\paragraph{Data and scope.}
CP annotations follow HarmThoughts~\citep{harmthoughts} without independent IAA evaluation; if annotation error is ${\geq}2$ steps, QwQ-32B's lead time ($-$1.2 to +1.9) falls within noise. We cover 2 architectures and 2 scales; intermediate scales, proprietary models, multi-turn and multilingual settings are untested. Results are correlational; causal intervention is needed to confirm mechanistic involvement.

